WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.849 --> 00:00:05.480
Game of Thrones Season 6 Episode 1 just came
out and some pretty crazy stuff happens so

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:06.850
let’s get into it.

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:09.550
We begin at the Wall with Jon dead in the
snow.

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:13.690
Davos and Ghost and some loyal Night’s Watchmen
are in conflict with Alliser Thorne, who seems

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:16.290
to be taking over the Watch after Jon’s
death.

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:19.840
Edd goes to get the wildlings – who probably
won’t be too happy when they hear what happened

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:20.840
to Jon.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:25.789
Melisandre comes and says she foresaw Jon
fighting at Winterfell, and, well, so have

00:00:25.789 --> 00:00:28.130
we – that’s probably him there in the
trailer.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:31.949
There’s heaps of evidence in the books and
the show that Jon will be back – “he always

00:00:31.949 --> 00:00:32.949
comes back”.

00:00:32.949 --> 00:00:37.730
The only questions are how and when and in
what he’ll be like when he rises.

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:43.170
But in the meantime, conflict is brewing with
Watchmen and wildlings and Davos.

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:47.449
In Winterfell, Ramsay is also mourning his
dead in his own special way – “feed her

00:00:47.449 --> 00:00:48.449
to the dogs”.

00:00:48.449 --> 00:00:52.239
Ramsay’s dad Roose reminds him that Sansa
is the Bolton’s best hope of controlling

00:00:52.239 --> 00:00:56.819
the north, and also that if Walda has a son,
that son would inherit Winterfell ahead of

00:00:56.819 --> 00:01:01.340
the bastard Ramsay, so some people think that
Ramsay might end up killing Walda and Roose

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:02.340
this season.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:07.690
Meanwhile, Theon and Sansa are hunted by Boltons,
Theon bravely risks his life to try to protect

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:11.070
her – which could hint at the beginning
of redemption for him – but the Boltons

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:15.460
close in, but Brienne and Pod appear to save
the day and carve up the Boltons.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:19.240
Sansa finally accepts Brienne’s service
and protection, which is a beautiful moment

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:22.840
for Brienne, mirroring her pledges to Renly
and Catelyn.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:26.479
Hopefully she’ll have better luck keeping
Sansa alive.

00:01:26.479 --> 00:01:30.450
In King’s Landing, Cersei is still reeling
from her walk of shame, and she’s crushed

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:33.689
even further when she finds out her daughter
Myrcella is dead.

00:01:33.689 --> 00:01:37.229
She talks about the prophecy of Maggy the
Frog, who said that Cersei’s kids would

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:38.229
die.

00:01:38.229 --> 00:01:40.929
It’s interesting that the show hasn’t
mentioned the other part of Maggy’s prophecy,

00:01:40.929 --> 00:01:45.140
that Cersei will be killed by her valonqar,
or little brother, which she thinks means

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:48.539
Tyrion, but some readers think means Jaime.

00:01:48.539 --> 00:01:52.969
In any case Jaime says fuck prophecy, fuck
everyone else, we will take everything back,

00:01:52.969 --> 00:01:56.030
which will put him at odds with the Faith.

00:01:56.030 --> 00:02:00.869
Here we see the High Sparrow and Septa Unella
playing good cop bad cop with Margaery Tyrell,

00:02:00.869 --> 00:02:03.319
who is still imprisoned along with her brother
Loras.

00:02:03.319 --> 00:02:06.909
Cersei is not exactly the biggest fan of the
Tyrells, so it’ll be interesting to see

00:02:06.909 --> 00:02:11.150
how much the Lannisters and Tyrells join forces
to face the Faith.

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:16.270
Down in Dorne, Ellaria and Tyene suddenly
kill Doran and Areo, and Obara and Nymeria

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:19.530
kill Trystane in King’s Landing, and this
is pretty crazy.

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:23.171
Cause the motivation of the Sand Snakes is
that they want to start a war against the

00:02:23.171 --> 00:02:27.370
Lannisters because the Lannisters, or rather
the Mountain, killed their father Oberyn,

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:29.580
and earlier, their aunt Elia.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:32.830
Doran tries to prevent war and that seems
to be why Ellaria kills him.

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:36.890
But isn’t it kinda crazy to kill Oberyn’s
family so you can avenge Oberyn?

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:41.690
Further, Ellaria and the Sand Snakes are all
bastards, with no rightful claim over Dorne

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:44.390
– will they even be able to take control?

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:47.890
Many book readers don’t like this change,
but maybe the show’s just cutting to the

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:52.180
chase, getting to the point, which is probably
that Dorne will war against the Lannisters,

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:57.160
and probably end up supporting the Targaryens
– Daenerys in the show, but maybe Aegon

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:58.470
in the books.

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:02.140
Also it’s cool to see Obara and Nymeria
in King’s Landing – might be they’ll

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:05.860
get in on the conflict, maybe they’ll kill
Tommen, as Nym threatens in the books.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:10.180
It might also make sense for them to go after
Robert Strong, the reanimated Mountain, ‘cause

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:14.180
after all, he’s the guy who killed Oberyn
and Elia.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:18.150
Varys and Tyrion rock some sweet capes, talk
about the rising political tension and the

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:22.060
threat of the Sons of the Harpy, and all this
doom and gloom looks to put Tyrion in a good

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:23.060
mood.

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:26.910
He’s really starting to shake off his earlier
depression, he’s getting back into the game,

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:30.350
so it’ll be great to watch what he and Varys
can accomplish together.

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:34.460
They pass a red priest preaching about Daenerys
being Azor Ahai, which is cool, and might

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:37.580
foreshadow the arrival of the priestess Kinvara
sometime later.

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:41.820
It’s interesting that the priest wears the
same hexagonal pattern we see on Melisandre

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:45.520
and Quaithe – maybe meaning this guy’s
from Asshai.

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:49.840
Finally we see Dany’s fleet burning in Slaver’s
Bay, and Tyrion’s all like, looks we won’t

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:53.840
be sailing to Westeros, but wouldn’t it
be convenient if we knew some friendly Vikings

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:55.850
who could bring Dany some ships…

00:03:55.850 --> 00:04:00.530
Meanwhile, Jorah and Daario search for Dany
in the Dothraki Sea, they have a bit of banter

00:04:00.530 --> 00:04:04.720
to stoke their rivalry, we see that Jorah’s
greyscale is getting pretty gnarly, and Dany’s

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.160
on the road to Vaes Dothrak, the Dothraki
city.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:12.210
Dany suffers the whips and harassment of her
captors, and keeps her cards close to her

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:15.730
chest, only revealing that she can speak Dothraki
when she’s brought before Khal Moro.

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:19.730
For a moment things look like they might turn
around, but then Dany finds out she’s expected

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:23.660
to join the dosh khaleen, the “widows of
dead khals”, who live out their days in

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:27.260
Vaes Dothrak, which is probably not what Dany
had in mind.

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:30.820
But in the books, Quaithe tells Dany that
“To go forward [she] must go back”, so

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:34.670
this return to the Dothraki could be crucial
in Dany’s arc moving forward.

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:38.140
She won’t want to hang around the Dothraki
forever though, so wouldn’t it be convenient

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:42.130
if we knew a friendly dragon who could fly
in to spirit her away…

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:45.740
In Braavos, Arya is still blind, and is begging
on the streets.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:48.520
You can briefly hear someone saying “after
what happened to that Kingsguard”, which

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:52.190
is a reference to Arya’s murder of Meryn
Trant last season, which is cool.

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:56.810
But anyway “the waif” turns up, and proceeds
to beat the absolute shit out of Arya, which

00:04:56.810 --> 00:05:00.570
is meant to train her to use all her senses,
though in real life that kind of beating would

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:04.150
give you a fractured skull before Daredevil
vision, but regardless this suffering will

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:06.430
probably make Arya stronger.

00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:10.290
Even so, there might come a day when Arya’s
had enough of the waif’s shit – so we

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:13.060
may soon see real conflict between the two.

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:16.930
One little thing in the books is that Arya
gets around being blind by warging into a

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:21.710
cat – entering into its consciousness and
seeing through its eyes, like Bran does with

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:22.710
Summer.

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:24.700
Hopefully they’ll include that in the show.

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:30.850
And then, back at the Wall, Melisandre reveals
her true form as a very very old woman, which…

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:32.250
actually makes a lot of sense.

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:36.240
It’s hinted in the show and the books that
Mel is older than she seems , that she’s

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:39.700
hiding her true appearance with a kind of
magic called a glamour.

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:43.280
The glamour seems to work using this ruby
at her neck, though she has been seen without

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:45.600
it before without looking old.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:49.300
Maybe that’s a continuity error, maybe the
magic works some other way, but the real point

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:53.420
here is that Melisandre’s nakedness shows
where she’s at as a character right now.

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:59.020
Remember, when we first met her, she seemed
so powerful, so beautiful, so certain . But

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:03.510
all of her hopes and beliefs were founded
on Stannis Baratheon being Azor Ahai, the

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:08.240
chosen one of the Lord of Light, and now that
he’s dead, she’s lost everything.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:13.860
Her nakedness is a moment of honesty and vulnerability
and humanity, from someone who’s now in

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:16.910
deep doubt over who she is and what she believes.

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:23.550
It’ll be amazing to see how she comes out
of this, and what it might mean for Jon Snow.

00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:27.010
So that is Episode 1 of Season 6 of Game of
Thrones.

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:30.810
We’ve gotta a lotta characters brought low,
beaten down, disempowered, disillusioned,

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:36.670
dead, but there’s also a strong sense of
rising for revenge, with Sansa, and Dorne,

00:06:36.670 --> 00:06:37.670
and the Lannisters.

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:42.139
We’ve got lots of women kicking ass, we’ve
got religions playing a part, we got magic,

00:06:42.139 --> 00:06:45.380
and politics, and everywhere tension is rising.

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:50.670
The stage is set, and for the most part, no
one knows what’s coming next.

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:51.670
Thanks for watching.

00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:54.760
If you’d like to see a breakdown like this
for every episode of Season 6, please let

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:58.870
us know by liking, sharing, subscribing, and
commenting what you want to see next.

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:02.760
You might like to check out our videos on
Thoros of Myr, a red priest like Mel who also

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:07.370
has a crisis of faith, and on Jon’s resurrection,
and on Arya’s character arc.

